<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Selim III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1761">1761</a>–<a href="/years/1808">1808</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Selim III was Ottoman sultan from 1789 to 1807. After defeats by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> he launched the Nizam-ı Cedid, a programme of military and fiscal reform built around a new European-style army, and opened permanent embassies in European capitals. His reforms were opposed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/janissaries">janissaries</a>, the ulema and provincial strongmen such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osman-pazvantoglu">Osman Pazvantoğlu</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vidin">Vidin</a>; he was deposed in 1807 and killed the following year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/selim-iii.jpg" alt="Selim III" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Konstantin Kapıdağlı · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Konstantin_Kapidagli_002.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
